Fail instead of crashing on 1D inputs to the oneDNN MatMul kernels.

The oneDNN EP rejects MatMul and MatMulInteger nodes with inputs of rank < 2,
but only when their shapes are known. Nodes with unknown input shapes are
accepted, and the kernels then assume matrices. For two 1D inputs
output_shape has a single dimension, so the broadcast loop

  for (size_t i = 0; i < output_shape.size() - 2; i++)

runs towards SIZE_MAX, reading and writing past the end of the vectors until
it hits an unmapped page.

MatmulIntegerOpTest.MatMulInteger_int8_1D_Vector_KDimensionMismatch, added in
https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime/commit/3b8482c00a8ead31f3870d3aba0ece76c162f2b1,
triggers this: it leaves the input shapes out of the graph, and oneDNN rejects
only the uint8 weights of the sibling test, not the int8 ones. With USE=onednn
the CPU EP fails as expected, then the oneDNN run crashes the whole
onnxruntime_provider_test binary. In the build directory:

  gdb -q -batch -ex run -ex bt --args ./onnxruntime_provider_test \
    --gtest_filter=MatmulIntegerOpTest.MatMulInteger_int8_1D_Vector_KDimensionMismatch

